#
# wifi.env.example -- template for the bench Wi-Fi credentials the
# `c6_wifi_join` firmware compiles in at BUILD time.
#
# Copy this file to `wifi.env` (which is gitignored) and fill it in, or export
# the same two variables in your shell. The root `just apps::build` recipe
# validates and loads `wifi.env` before CMake, which compiles the values into
# the image. With neither set the image still builds -- it prints a runtime FAIL
# instead of baking a blank credential -- so a credential is NEVER committed and
# the aggregate cross-build stays green.
#
#   cp wifi.env.example wifi.env      # then edit wifi.env
#
# The passphrase is not stored here in the real bench setup; it lives in OpenBao
# at secret/ra8d2/bench-network (key bench_psk). Pull it at build time, e.g.:
#
#   export RA8_C6_WIFI_SSID=ra8-bench
#   export RA8_C6_WIFI_PSK="$(python3 scripts/secrets/openbao_client.py \
#       get secret/ra8d2/bench-network bench_psk)"
#   just apps::build ek_ra8d2::hw_validated::c6::c6_wifi_join
#
# KEEP THIS FILE PURE KEY=value (source-able; no shebang, no logic).

# The bench SSID (2.4 GHz; the ESP32-C6 is a 2.4 GHz single-band radio).
RA8_C6_WIFI_SSID=

# The WPA2 passphrase. Leave both values empty for a credential-free build.
RA8_C6_WIFI_PSK=
